    "durationMs": 421003,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What was built** (Rails 8.0.2 API-only, Ruby 3.4.3, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`):\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` (URL stored verbatim; unique base58 code generated when omitted), 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for missing/invalid url, invalid code, or malformed JSON\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 or 404 JSON; `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with `Location` and an atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` increment; `GET /links` → `{items, total}` in ascending creation order\n- `Link` model with URL/code format validation, unique index on `code`, and collision-safe code generation\n- `start.sh` (executable): runs `rails db:prepare` (creates the DB on first boot, applies pending migrations), then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- README with a \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Key issues found and fixed along the way:**\n- The `json` gem 3.x removed `quirks_mode`, which Rails 8.0.2's JSON param parsing still passes — every JSON request was 500ing. Pinned `json ~> 2.9.1` in the Gemfile.\n- Rails 8's default production `force_ssl` would have 301'd all plain-HTTP test traffic — disabled it.\n- Duplicate codes initially returned 422 because `errors.added?` doesn't match validator types in Rails 8 — switched to checking `errors.details` directly.\n\n**Verification:** a 40-check HTTP test suite passes (all endpoints, status codes, exact response shapes, malformed/edge-case JSON, boundary 4/20-char codes), click counts and links survive server restarts, and a cold start against a brand-new database name provisions the schema and works end-to-end. The bench database is left empty and port 8000 is free for the harness."
  }
